Summary:
# Motivation:
The boot tests are not passing in CI because this address value should be generated dynamically by querying hvf.

https://www.internalfb.com/code/arvr-qemu/[stable-9.2-meta]/
```
Here's the chain:

  1. include/hw/arm/virt.h:185 — The selector macro:
  #define VIRT_ECAM_ID(high) (high ? VIRT_HIGH_PCIE_ECAM : VIRT_PCIE_ECAM)
  2. hw/arm/virt.c:190 — Low/compact ECAM address:
  [VIRT_PCIE_ECAM] = { 0x3f000000, 0x01000000 },
  3. hw/arm/virt.c:214 — High ECAM (base computed dynamically):
  [VIRT_HIGH_PCIE_ECAM] = { 0x0, 256 * MiB },
  4. hw/arm/virt.c:3298 — Default: highmem_ecam starts as true (for machine >= 3.0):
  vms->highmem_ecam = !vmc->no_highmem_ecam;
  5. hw/arm/virt.c:2400 — Gated on firmware + arch:
  vms->highmem_ecam &= (!firmware_loaded || aarch64);
  6. hw/arm/virt.c:1825 — The critical check in virt_set_high_memmap:
  fits = (region_base + region_size) <= BIT_ULL(pa_bits);
  *region_enabled &= fits;
  6. If the high ECAM address doesn't fit in the IPA (physical address bits), highmem_ecam gets set to false → falls back to 0x3f000000.
  7. hw/arm/virt.c:1858 — And pa_bits comes from:
  if (!vms->highmem) { pa_bits = 32; }
  7. Otherwise pa_bits comes from the HVF IPA size (target/arm/hvf/hvf.c:934-948):
  hv_vm_config_get_default_ipa_size(&default_ipa_size);

  So: HVF queries the chip → IPA too small → high ECAM doesn't fit → falls back to 0x3f000000. Different Apple Silicon chips (M1 vs M2 vs M3) can report different default IPA sizes.
```

previously modified here: D80563549
